Enhancement: snapshot labels, descriptions, delete protection and rich filters

Snapshots can now carry a `label`, a `description`, and delete protection.
`backup` sets them via `--label`, `--description`/`--description-from` and
`--delete-never`/`--delete-after <duration>`; `tag` can change them afterwards
with `--set-label`, `--set-description` and `--set-delete never|none|<dur>`.
The metadata uses the same JSON keys as rustic, so both tools agree on it.

`forget`/`prune` keep delete-protected snapshots regardless of the retention
policy (a count of kept snapshots is printed); the new
`--override-delete-protection` flag removes them anyway.

All snapshot-selecting commands gained the rustic-compatible extended filters
`--filter-label`, `--filter-paths-exact`, `--filter-tags-exact`,
`--filter-after`/`--filter-before`, `--filter-size`, `--filter-size-added` and
`--filter-last`, and snapshot references now accept the `latest~N` syntax to
address the N-th latest matching snapshot. `snapshots` shows a `Label` column
for labeled snapshots and `label` is available as a `--group-by` key.

